# Supported APIs first

Exhaust supported Paper APIs before reflection, NMS, or bytecode transformation.

# Reflection / NMS

Requires an architecture decision record with:

- Capability enabled
- Why public APIs are insufficient
- Version assumptions and failure mode
- Test plan

Do not spread reflection across hot event paths.

# Java agent (optional)

The standard plugin and client mods must remain useful without an agent.

An agent must:

- Be a separate artifact (`eventlens-agent` on Paper, `eventlens-client-agent` on NeoForge/Forge)
- Load only with `-javaagent` at JVM startup
- Never self-attach by default
- Transform only exact allowlisted targets with signature verification
- Perform additive observation-only changes
- Fail closed on mismatch
- Expose a narrow versioned protocol via `eventlens-observability`
- Stop producing data when no trace session requires it

Do not attach the Paper agent to Minecraft, or share NeoForge transforms with Fabric.

Agent tests must run in forked JVMs.

# Current status

- Paper: `eventlens-agent` wraps `RegisteredListener.callEvent` (ADR 0001)
- Client: `eventlens-client-agent` wraps NeoForge game-bus `invoke(Event)` and Forge `ASMEventHandler.invoke(Event)` (ADR 0003); Fabric is not implemented
- Shared protocol: `eventlens-observability` (Java 21 bytecode)
- No NMS usage

A new transform requires an approved ADR and preservation tests.
